course: dictionary
lesson: 10538
title: The ulna
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The ulna is one of the two long bones in your forearm. It runs from your elbow down to your wrist, on the little-finger side of your arm.
explain: The other forearm bone is the radius, on the thumb side. Scientists and doctors name the two bones together as the radius and ulna, and they work as a pair.
explain: «Now turn a door handle: your hand flips palm up and palm down because one forearm bone, the radius, rolls over the other, the ulna.» Turning your hand is possible because these two bones can twist around each other.
fact: The ulna is a long bone in the forearm.
fact: The ulna sits between the elbow and the wrist, on the little-finger side.
fact: «The forearm has two bones, the radius on the thumb side and the ulna on the little-finger side.»
fact: The bony tip of your elbow is the top of the ulna.
fact: A broken forearm may mean a fractured ulna or radius.
exercise: «The forearm has two bones, the radius on the thumb side and the ulna on the little-finger side.» Which side of your arm is the ulna on? | The thumb side | *The little-finger side | The top of the wrist | The inside of the elbow
exercise: Where is the ulna? | Between the wrist and the fingers | In the upper arm | Between the shoulder and the elbow | *Between the elbow and the wrist
exercise: When you turn your hand palm up, which bone rolls over the other? | The ulna | The humerus | The wrist | *The radius
test: Which bone forms the bony tip of your elbow? | The radius | The wrist | *The ulna | A finger bone
test: A broken forearm may mean a fractured ... | *The ulna or radius | The skull | The finger | The elbow
exam: Which statement about the ulna is true? | The ulna is in the upper arm | *The ulna is one of the two long bones in the forearm | The ulna is a bone in the leg | The ulna is on the thumb side of the forearm
